problem:
Find all surjective functions  $f:\mathbb{N}\to\mathbb{N}$  such that for all positive integers  $a$  and  $b$ , exactly one of the following equations is true:
\begin{align*}
f(a)&=f(b), <br /> 
 f(a+b)&=\min\{f(a),f(b)\}.
\end{align*}
*Remarks:*  $\mathbb{N}$  denotes the set of all positive integers. A function  $f:X\to Y$  is said to be surjective if for every  $y\in Y$  there exists  $x\in X$  such that  $f(x)=y$ .

Determine if it is possible to color each of the rational numbers either red or blue such that the following three conditions are all satisfied:

(i) \( x \) and \( -x \) are opposite colors, for all rational \( x \neq 0 \);

(ii) \( x \) and \( 1-x \) are opposite colors, for all rational \( x \neq \frac{1}{2} \);

(iii) \( x \) and \( \frac{1}{x} \) are opposite colors, for all rational \( x \neq 0, \pm1 \).

Find all functions \( f: \mathbb{Z} \rightarrow \mathbb{Z} \) that satisfy the following conditions for any prime number \( p \):
1. \( f(p) > 0 \);
2. For all \( x \in \mathbb{Z} \),
\[ p \mid \left((f(x) + f(p))^{f(p)} - x \right). \}

Determine all positive integers \( n \) for which there exists a set \( S \) with the following properties:

(i) \( S \) consists of \( n \) positive integers, all smaller than \( 2^{n-1} \);

(ii) for any two distinct subsets \( A \) and \( B \) of \( S \), the sum of the elements of \( A \) is different from the sum of the elements of \( B \).
